### 1) Generar token
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123"
}

### Guardar el token en una variable (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ)
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 2) Crear orden (nace en CREATED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "numeroOrden": "ORD-0001",
  "idCliente": 1001,
  "tipoServicio": "INSTALACION_INTERNET"
}

### 3) Listar ordenes
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Consultar orden por id
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Actualizar estado: CREATED -> VALIDATED
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes/1/estado
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "estado": "VALIDATED",
  "observacion": "Documentos verificados"
}

### 6) Transicion invalida (VALIDATED -> COMPLETED) => 409
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes/1/estado
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "estado": "COMPLETED"
}

### 7) Historial de la orden
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes/1/historial
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8) Sin token => 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ordenes
